invariant: INV-48
file: mlkem.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: mlkem_decaps_cpu runs mlkem.c's decapsulation whatever the value
  says, so a session with CH_CPU_AVX2 re-encrypts on sha3.c alone.
  The bytes are the same. bin/x86_kernels_test counts the copy's
  calls under every ch_cfg.cpu value, and test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh
  builds it for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips
  without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
        mlkem_decaps_avx2(widemul, ss, ct, dk);
--- new
        mlkem_decaps(widemul, ss, ct, dk);
